### Test OTP Endpoints

### 1. Register a new user (should send OTP)
POST http://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test123!@#",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "role": "student",
  "department": "Computer Science",
  "semester": 1
}

### 2. Verify OTP (replace with actual OTP from email/console)
POST http://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 3. Resend OTP
POST http://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

### 4. Test login (should fail if not verified)
POST http://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test123!@#"
}

### 5. Health check
GET http://localhost:5001/health
